          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "When you are augmenting an existing ERP rather than replacing it, you need a partner that specializes in **\"surround-and-extend\" architecture**. You want consultants who understand manufacturing shop-floor realities (rugged tablets, barcode scanning, offline mode), document extraction (AI Builder for incoming POs), and how to safely bridge legacy databases/APIs without causing data corruption.\n\nThe top Sydney-based and Australian Microsoft Power Platform and automation consultancies best suited for this brief include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Mid-Market ERP & Power Platform Specialists\n*These firms have deep ERP roots, meaning they understand chart of accounts, BOMs, routing, and work orders, but also run modern Power Platform practices to build layers on top.*\n\n* **Professional Advantage** (North Sydney)\n  * **Best for:** Safe ERP integrations and mid-market manufacturing workflows.\n  * **Why them:** They have decades of experience with both ERP engines and Microsoft Cloud applications. They have a dedicated Power Platform and Process Automation practice experienced in building staging layers between modern frontends and core operational databases.\n* **Eagle360 Consulting** (Sydney & Melbourne)\n  * **Best for:** Pragmatic, mid-market manufacturing automation.\n  * **Why them:** Specializes heavily in eliminating spreadsheets, paper travelers, and duplicate entry. They frequently build Power Apps for warehouse/floor scanning and order ingestion, connecting back into mid-tier ERPs via APIs or custom connectors.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Specialist Power Platform & Intelligent Automation Partners\n*These firms are elite Microsoft low-code specialists. They are ideal if you want clean UI/UX for floor staff, sophisticated AI-driven order extraction, and governance.*\n\n* **Barhead Solutions** (Sydney CBD)\n  * **Best for:** Complex process automation, AI Builder, and custom connector development.\n  * **Why them:** One of Microsoft’s premier Business Applications partners in Australia. They excel at complex workflow orchestration using Power Automate, AI Builder (for extracting order data from emailed PDFs), and building Custom Connectors to proprietary on-premise systems.\n* **Rapid Circle** (Sydney presence)\n  * **Best for:** Frontline worker enablement and low-code governance.\n  * **Why them:** They have a strong reputation for designing touch-friendly, intuitive Power Apps for frontline staff (operators, pickers, machine technicians) while setting up proper Application Lifecycle Management (ALM) and Center of Excellence (CoE) governance.\n* **Intergy Consulting** (Sydney)\n  * **Best for:** Custom API bridging and legacy systems.\n  * **Why them:** They operate as a hybrid between a custom software house and a Microsoft solutions partner. If your ERP is older (e.g., legacy on-premise SQL or lacking modern REST APIs), their engineering team can build the middleware or API gateway needed for Power Apps to talk to it cleanly.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Industrial Data & Operations Specialists\n* **BizData** (Sydney / Melbourne)\n  * **Best for:** Shop-floor telemetry, machine data capture, and operational reporting.\n  * **Why them:** If your shop-floor data capture needs to bridge both human input (operator check-sheets on Power Apps) and machine output (OEE, SCADA/PLC counters, downtime tracking) into Power BI dashboards alongside ERP data.\n\n---\n\n### What to Ask When Interviewing These Partners\n\nBecause your primary constraint is **not replacing the ERP**, screen candidates on these four technical areas:\n\n1. **ERP Integration Strategy:**\n   * *Ask:* *\"How do you plan to interface with our ERP?\"*\n   * *Look for:* If your ERP has modern REST APIs, they should propose a **Custom Connector** using Microsoft Dataverse or Azure API Management. If it's an on-premise SQL-based ERP, they should discuss the **On-Premises Data Gateway** with a staging database. If it has no API, ask how they use **Power Automate Desktop (RPA)** to emulate data entry without corrupting database integrity.\n2. **AI-Driven Order Ingestion:**\n   * *Ask:* *\"How will you handle non-standard customer purchase orders received via email?\"*\n   * *Look for:* Experience deploying **Power Automate + AI Builder Document Processing**. They should design a \"human-in-the-loop\" exception screen (Power Apps) where an order clerk can review line items that fall below a confidence threshold before pushing into the ERP.\n3. **Shop-Floor Hardware & UX Realities:**\n   * *Ask:* *\"How do you design Power Apps for factory floor environments?\"*\n   * *Look for:* Awareness of touch targets for gloved hands, barcode scanning (using native device cameras vs. hardware integration with Zebra/Honeywell scanners), and **Power Apps Offline capability** (crucial if your warehouse or plant has Wi-Fi dead spots).\n4. **Microsoft Licensing Architecture:**\n   * *Ask:* *\"How do you optimize licensing so we don't pay enterprise prices for every shop-floor user?\"*\n   * *Look for:* Deep knowledge of Power Apps *Per App* vs. *Per User* plans, Pay-as-you-go via Azure, or Microsoft 365 frontline worker (F3) licensing, alongside compliance regarding Microsoft’s multiplexing rules.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ],
